# Claude Code per-session worktrees. Already in .git/info/exclude, but that file is
# invisible to codegraph: its buildDefaultIgnore() (extraction/index.js) seeds the
# watcher's chokidar `ignored` predicate from the built-in defaults plus THIS file
# only -- it never reads .git/info/exclude, nested .gitignores, or core.excludesFile.
# The indexer, by contrast, enumerates via `git ls-files -o --exclude-standard`, which
# DOES honor info/exclude. So watch scope and index scope diverged exactly here: on
# 2026-09-06 the agent-src daemon was watching 20 live worktrees (20,224 dirs / ~104k
# source files it could never index, plus each one's Electron release/win-unpacked
# build output -- the root-anchored `apps/desktop/release/` rule does not match at
# `.claude/worktrees/<name>/apps/desktop/release/`). Every file event in any worktree
# schedules a FULL-project reconcile (CodeGraph.watch()'s syncFn calls sync() with no
# changed-file argument), which cost 1.5-142s each against the 1.07 GB graph. Handles
# climbed ~3,750/min to a ~174,300 ceiling. That is NOT a leak: ~3,750/min is just
# chokidar's normal crawl rate, and the crawl never CONVERGED, because 20 worktrees
# churned (Electron rebuilds, git ops, 20 agents writing) faster than it could settle.
# Measured: one daemon at 91% of a core and 174,304 handles over 4h. Post-fix the same
# code converges to ~8,720 handles in ~4min and holds -- verified flat over 13h at 0.26%
# of a core (2026-09-07). Diagnose this class by CONVERGENCE (sample repeatedly, ask
# whether the count goes FLAT), never by comparing one snapshot against a directory
# count. Only takes effect for daemons STARTED AFTER this rule lands -- ignoreMatcher
# is built once, at watcher startup.
**/.claude/worktrees/

# Web UI build output
hermes_cli/web_dist/
# Cross-process web UI build lock (flock target, always empty)
.web_ui_build.lock
apps/desktop/build/
apps/desktop/dist/

# tsc-emitted artifacts (a stray `tsc -b` compiles into src/, and vite then
# resolves the stale .js OVER the .tsx — never track these)
apps/desktop/src/**/*.js
apps/desktop/src/**/*.js.map
apps/desktop/src/**/*.d.ts
# EXCEPT bundled plain-ESM plugin entries (adopted SDK-consumer plugins,
# e.g. hermes-bots): plugin.js IS the source, not tsc output. No .tsx
# sibling exists, so the stale-shadow hazard above cannot apply.
!apps/desktop/src/plugins/*/plugin.js
!apps/desktop/src/global.d.ts
!apps/desktop/src/vite-env.d.ts

